Spec: Lesson entity

Purpose:
  The Lesson entity: a date, a start time and an end time, a topic, free-text notes and a reference to a
  CourseRealization. A view-less, route-less package used by ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  ../semester/semester.sdd and ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd

Must:
  A Lesson has a date, a start time and an end time, a topic, free-text notes and a reference to a CourseRealization.
  @LessonRepository in ./ports.py exposes operations to list lessons for a CourseRealization or a date range and to
  add one.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist.

Tasks:
  [?] Decide whether a Lesson can be deleted or edited after creation, and whether more than one Lesson may exist
    for the same day and CourseRealization
  [x] Implement @Lesson in ./domain.py and a hardcoded ./services.py returning placeholder Lessons for each
    placeholder CourseRealization across the hardcoded Semester, standing in for @LessonRepository until
    persistence exists
  [x] Replace the hardcoded ./services.py with a class-based @LessonRepository-backed `LessonService`
    (./ports.py and ./repository_sqlite.py), per ../architecture.sdd's Example
